      "class_code": 22,
      "payload": {
        "name": "pc-check-retry-eligibility",
        "description": "Deterministic pure-logic guard that returns whether a logical step invocation is eligible for a bounded retry, before any dispatch is considered. It is evidence-conditioned pure logic, not dispatch permission: it never grants Tool permission, does not replace live instance-wide Tool policy, current global allow/block settings, cancellation, stale-attempt fencing, resource limits or actual deduplication evidence. It only reports eligibility from declared inputs; a true result still requires a fresh valid attempt and current policy admission at the actual dispatch boundary. Missing, null or invalid data fails closed. Typed inputs are a target interface; the typed-runner and Monty execution gap remain an explicit prerequisite. No I/O, imports or host calls.",
        "content": "def check_retry_eligibility(operation_state, outcome, attempt, max_attempts, read_only, dedup_verified):
    if not isinstance(operation_state, str) or operation_state not in ('completed', 'unknown', 'not_started'):
        return {'retry': False}
    if outcome not in ('retryable', 'terminal'):
        return {'retry': False}
    if not isinstance(attempt, int) or isinstance(attempt, bool) or attempt <= 0:
        return {'retry': False}
    if not isinstance(max_attempts, int) or isinstance(max_attempts, bool) or max_attempts <= 0:
        return {'retry': False}
    if not isinstance(read_only, bool) or not isinstance(dedup_verified, bool):
        return {'retry': False}
    if outcome != 'retryable':
        return {'retry': False}
    if attempt >= max_attempts:
        return {'retry': False}
    if operation_state == 'completed':
        return {'retry': False}
    if not (read_only or dedup_verified):
        return {'retry': False}
    return {'retry': True}"
      }
    }
  ],
  "composition_summary": "Proposed one class-22 pure-logic component pc-check-retry-eligibility. It reads raw candidate inputs with presence/type checks (operation_state, outcome, attempt, max_attempts, read_only, dedup_verified) and returns {'retry': boolean} at module scope, failing closed on missing/null/invalid data. True only when outcome is retryable, attempt < max_attempts, state is not completed, and read_only OR dedup_verified is true. Completed effects never replay. The body makes zero host calls and no I/O/imports. The description retains the live policy/cancellation/resource checks and typed-runner gap; this guard is evidence-conditioned pure logic, not dispatch permission. No adjusted volatile messages, bridge messages, recipe updates, intent examples or settings changes were made; the volatile tail was preserved unchanged.",
